</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Buckner was a different kind of prospect: <strong>6-foot-7 and 291 pounds</strong> with 34⅜-inch arms and an 11¾-inch hand. He ran a 5.05 40 at the 2016 combine, but the number that matters for a defensive tackle is the first 10 yards, and his <strong>1.77-second 10-yard split</strong> showed real burst for a man that size. He added a 32-inch vertical, a 9-foot-8 broad jump, a 4.47 short shuttle and a 7.51 three-cone.</p>
<p>San Francisco took him seventh overall. He spent four seasons there, recording 28.5 sacks, before the 49ers traded him to Indianapolis in 2020 for a first-round pick. He's a three-time Pro Bowler with first- and second-team All-Pro selections, and he has 75.5 career sacks heading into his return.</p>
